      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. WILLIAMS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The factfinding at issue in this case is significantly different than the factfinding at issue in this Court's recent Sixth Amendment cases, in which the Court struck down changes in sentencing practice that had the effect of removing factfinding from the province of the jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-901",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "90ac0511db297b5d91ed653eca6b842b4f29f520df6254f7839861152ddbab9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90ac0511db29-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How many others? Do you know?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-901",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "90ac0511db297b5d91ed653eca6b842b4f29f520df6254f7839861152ddbab9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90ac0511db29-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What if the -- what if the rule were that all sentences should be concurrent unless the defendant has been convicted of a prior federal offense and then the sentence runs consecutive to the federal sentence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-901",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "90ac0511db297b5d91ed653eca6b842b4f29f520df6254f7839861152ddbab9d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-90ac0511db29-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Lannet, one of the -- or perhaps the driving force behind Apprendi was the fear of abuse by a combination of the charging power and the sentencing power. What abuse do you see if -- if you lose this case? What potential abuse?"
    },
